# What Docker must not copy into the build context.
#
# The context for every image is this folder, because the training job needs
# data/california_housing.csv and the drift job needs data/reference.csv. This
# file keeps the context small and keeps local files out of the images.

# Virtual environments and caches. They are large and belong to the machine
# they were made on.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.cache/

# Tests and the local Python pin. The images only ship the packages.
**/tests
**/.python-version

# Documentation, infrastructure and CI. None of it runs inside an image.
docs/
gitops/
terraform/
scripts/
**/*.md
.gitlab-ci.yml
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore

# Local settings. Nothing that can hold a secret is ever copied.
.env
.env.*

# macOS
**/.DS_Store
